Matrix Algebra:

> x12 _ matrix(1:4, 2, 2)
> x12   
     [,1] [,2] 
[1,]    1    3
[2,]    2    4
> x12 * x12
     [,1] [,2] 
[1,]    1    9
[2,]    4   16

Matrix Multiplication:

> x12 %*% x12
     [,1] [,2] 
[1,]    7   15
[2,]   10   22

Transpose:

> t (x12)
     [,1] [,2] 
[1,]    1    2
[2,]    3    4

Inverse:

> solve (x12)
     [,1] [,2] 
[1,]   -2  1.5
[2,]    1 -0.5

> x12 %*% solve(x12)
             [,1]          [,2] 
[1,] 1.000000e+00 -4.440892e-16
[2,] 8.881784e-16  1.000000e+00

Apply a Function to Sections of an Array
(MARGIN parameter: 1 indicates rows and 2 indicates columns):

> apply (x12, 1, exp)
          [,1]      [,2] 
[1,]  2.718282  7.389056
[2,] 20.085537 54.598150
> apply (x12, 2, exp)
         [,1]     [,2] 
[1,] 2.718282 20.08554
[2,] 7.389056 54.59815


